From 56345cea6a30dc7a1b036d5fb7900434b4a4c5e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Griffin Kroah-Hartman <griffin@kroah.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 16:23:27 +0200
Subject: nfc: nxp-nci: Add remove on IRQ error
Mime-version: 1.0
Content-type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-transfer-encoding: 8bit
Git-commit: 56345cea6a30dc7a1b036d5fb7900434b4a4c5e8
Patch-mainline: v7.3-rc1
References: stable-fixes

Add a call to nxp_nci_remove() in nxp_nci_i2c_probe() when the
request_threaded_irq() fails.
Previously, IRQ resources were not being freed upon error.

Assisted-by: gkh_clanker_2000
Cc: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Cc: Carl Lee <carl.lee@amd.com>
Cc: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
Cc: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com>
Cc: Ian Ray <ian.ray@gehealthcare.com>
Cc: "Uwe Kleine-König (The Capable Hub)" <u.kleine-koenig@baylibre.com>
Signed-off-by: Griffin Kroah-Hartman <griffin@kroah.com>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Reviewed-by: Ian Ray <ian.ray@gehealthcare.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/2026070726-observer-fang-9716@gregkh
Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
@@ -307,8 +307,10 @@ static int nxp_nci_i2c_probe(struct i2c_
 				 nxp_nci_i2c_irq_thread_fn,
 				 IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING | IRQF_ONESHOT,
 				 NXP_NCI_I2C_DRIVER_NAME, phy);
-	if (r < 0)
+	if (r < 0) {
 		nfc_err(&client->dev, "Unable to register IRQ handler\n");
+		nxp_nci_remove(phy->ndev);
+	}
 
 	return r;
 }
